      <h2>The Georgia Open Records Act</h2>

      <p>
        O.C.G.A. 50-18-71(a) says: "All public records shall be open for
        personal inspection and copying," subject to exemptions. Section
        50-18-71(b)(1)(A) says records are to be provided "within a reasonable
        amount of time not to exceed three business days of receipt of a
        request". If records are not available then, the agency must give a
        description and a timeline. That is not a guarantee that everything is
        delivered in three days. The Georgia law applies to Georgia agency
        records. It does not set a deadline for court dockets or for Alabama.
      </p>

